#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347121 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1889f67-327c-5e6e-b646-5bd58a244778" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing and Evaluating Triple Integrals Over Type III Regions From Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b963e54-2a6d-5390-85aa-5497fbe463b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347123} {:answer/id #uuid "dea7fc24-92d0-5e08-9ecd-a77026bf3cd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347124} {:answer/id #uuid "a5ee89e1-3e99-549a-ac53-49cecb1928e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347125} {:answer/id #uuid "a8a398ae-60de-53a1-97d5-832bfae3dc02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347126} {:answer/id #uuid "0e66dbf6-f123-5228-a62f-8a6d4fd98534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dea7fc24-92d0-5e08-9ecd-a77026bf3cd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347124} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5897bce-0eb1-5952-a21a-a34b1a1b4b1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347122}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "64c7d2bc-c812-5ad8-9b28-e90df9b77237" :question/math-academy-id "q-161836" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/assets/b6d469b24061f0f7284691b2e2f26a2c28d9557ab72a1c8ba3cad93eb65dde91.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}2{z}^{2}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/assets/9190139502ef900218e3c3b186295627af2a1370b9f7d789366dac6474251b54.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{x}{3}-z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/assets/aa02840c9fa15e5e5048608fff81ad9f0a5623821a57366bf12ec6d60332bc9e.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{x}{3}-z}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3-x/3-z}2{z}^{2}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3-x/3-z}2{z}^{2}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3-x/3-z}2{z}^{2}\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{z}^{2}[y]_{y=0}^{y=3-x/3-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{z}^{2}(3-\\frac{x}{3}-z)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(6{z}^{2}-\\frac{2}{3}x{z}^{2}-2{z}^{3})\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(6{z}^{2}-\\frac{2}{3}x{z}^{2}-2{z}^{3})\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}(6{z}^{2}-\\frac{2}{3}x{z}^{2}-2{z}^{3})\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[2{z}^{3}-\\frac{2}{9}x{z}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(8-\\frac{16}{9}x)\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(8-\\frac{16}{9}x)\\,dx & ={[8x-\\frac{16}{18}{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=3} \\\\  & =(24-8)-0 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
